App/SampleData/aava-n2k-3min.jsonl
  The first 3 minutes of the NMEA 2000 sample recording "aava-n2k.data" from the
  Signal K server project (https://github.com/SignalK/signalk-server), converted to
  Signal K deltas with canboatjs and n2k-signalk.
  Signal K server, canboatjs and n2k-signalk are licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
  The values "steering.rudderAngle" (source "simulated.rudder") are not part of the
  recording. They are simulated by Scripts/add-simulated-rudder.py.
  The own "navigation.rateOfTurn" values (source "simulated.rateOfTurn") are not part of the
  recording either. They are calculated from the recorded heading by
  Scripts/add-simulated-rate-of-turn.py.
  The engine values "propulsion.port.*" and "propulsion.starboard.*" (source
  "simulated.engines") are not part of the recording. They are simulated by
  Scripts/add-simulated-engines.py.
  The first line (a Signal K hello message) declares the own vessel as MMSI 230035780.
  This is deduced from the data: that AIS target reports the same position as the own GPS,
  so it is the own transponder.
